## **COMPREHENSIVE FIX: Room Main Thread Database Access Issues**

### ** Critical Issues Resolved:**

The app was crashing with `IllegalStateException: Cannot access database on the main thread` due to multiple synchronous database calls in ViewModels during Activity initialization.

### ** Root Causes Found & Fixed:**

#### **1. AuthViewModel Constructor Issue:**
```java
// ❌ BEFORE: Synchronous DB calls during ViewModel initialization
private void initializeAuthState() {
 if (authRepository.hasActiveSession()) { // DB call on main thread!
 authStateLiveData.setValue(AuthState.AUTHENTICATED);
 } else if (authRepository.isDeviceRegistered()) { // DB call on main thread!
 authStateLiveData.setValue(AuthState.DEVICE_REGISTERED);
 }
}

// ✅ AFTER: Fully async initialization
private void initializeAuthStateAsync() {
 authRepository.hasActiveSessionAsync().thenAccept(hasActiveSession -> {
 if (hasActiveSession) {
 authStateLiveData.postValue(AuthState.AUTHENTICATED);
 } else {
 authRepository.isDeviceRegisteredAsync().thenAccept(isRegistered -> {
 authStateLiveData.postValue(isRegistered ? 
 AuthState.DEVICE_REGISTERED : AuthState.NOT_AUTHENTICATED);
 });
 }
 });
}
```

#### **2. Activity Direct ViewModel Method Calls:**
```java
