## **Minimal Service Account Permissions**

```bash
# Create the service account
gcloud iam service-accounts create mobile-app-client \
 --display-name="Mobile App Client" \
 --description="Service account for EasyDelivery mobile applications"

# Grant Cloud Run access (to call your API endpoints)
gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding easydelivery-433910 \
 --member="serviceAccount:mobile-app-client@easydelivery-433910.iam.gserviceaccount.com" \
 --role="roles/run.invoker"

# Grant Firebase Storage access (for photos/signatures)
gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding easydelivery-433910 \
 --member="serviceAccount:mobile-app-client@easydelivery-433910.iam.gserviceaccount.com" \
 --role="roles/storage.objectAdmin"

# Generate the key
gcloud iam service-accounts keys create mobile-app-key.json \
 --iam-account=mobile-app-client@easydelivery-433910.iam.gserviceaccount.com
```

## **That's It! Only 2 Roles:**

### **1. `roles/run.invoker`**
- Allows calling your Cloud Run API endpoints
- All Firestore access goes through your API
- Perfect for authentication, device registration, trip management

### **2. `roles/storage.objectAdmin`** 
- Upload photos/signatures to Firebase Storage
- Read/write/delete objects in Cloud Storage buckets
- Essential for delivery proof of delivery

## **Security Benefits:**

✅ **No direct Firestore access** - all data operations through your API 
✅ **Audit trail** - all database changes logged through your API 
✅ **Centralized business logic** - validation happens in one place 
✅ **Easy to modify permissions** - just update your API, not mobile apps 
✅ **Firestore security rules irrelevant** - API controls everything 

## **Architecture Flow:**
```
Mobile App ──(Service Account Auth)──> Cloud Run API ──> Firestore
 │
 └──(Service Account Auth)──> Firebase Storage
```

## **What Your API Will Handle:**
- Device enrollment/registration
- Driver authentication 
- Session management
- Trip/delivery data
- All business logic and validation

## **What Mobile App Handles Directly:**
- Photo/signature uploads to Firebase Storage
- File management and cleanup

This is the **gold standard** for secure mobile app architecture! Once you create the service account with these permissions and share the JSON, I'll implement the authentication flow."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"
